CITY CONTRACT NO.
PROFESSIONAL SERVICES AGREEMENT
PREAMBLE
This
Agreement
(“Agreement”)
is
made
and
entered
into
this
day
of
2018, by and between the City of Cheyenne, a municipal corporation
organized under the laws of the State of Wyoming, located at 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne,
Wyoming 82001 (“City”), and the Cheyenne Youth Baseball League, located at P.O. Box 1401,
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82003-1401 (“the Contractor” and referred to collectively as, “Parties”).
RECITALS
WHEREAS, the City has the authority under the laws ofthe State of Wyoming to enter into
agreements with regards to real property upon terms and for such purposes as are in the public
interest;
WHEREAS, the City desires to enter into a service agreement whereby the Contractor will
provide food and beverage concessionaire services, more filly described herein, to members of the
public at certain recreational facilities located throughout the City at City-owned facilities, such
specific recreational facilities to be identified herein;
WHEREAS, the City solicited bids for contractors to provide the aforementioned services,
and the Contractor submitted a responsible and qualified bid to provide the required services to
members of the public; and
WHEREAS, it is the mutual desire of both the City and the Contractor to enter into this
Agreement in accordance with the terms stated hereinafter.
AGREEMENT
NOW, THEREFORE, for and in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements
herein contained, the Parties agree as follows:
1.
FACILITIES COVERED BY THIS AGREEMENT. The City hereby grants the
Contractor the right to use the concession stands within the Dutcher Baseball Complex, located at
4212 Converse Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming.
2.
ACCEPTANCE OF FACILITIES. Neither the City nor its agents have made any
warranties or representations with respect to the facilities, except as expressly set forth herein, and
no rights, easements, or licenses are acquired by the Contractor, by implication or otherwise, except
as expressly set forth in this Agreement. The acceptance of the facilities by the Contractor shall be
conclusive evidence that the Contractor accepts the facilities “as is” and that the facilities are in
good condition at the time of this Agreement.
1
