3.
TERM. The term of this Agreement shall commence on April 1, 2018 and shall
terminate on November 1, 2018, unless sooner canceled or terminated as hereinafter provided. At
the conclusion of the term stated herein, the Contractor and the City may renew for annual terms,
not to exceed three (3) optional renewals, but only upon mutual agreement of the Parties reached
no later than the anniversary of the commencement date stated in this numbered section of this
Agreement.
4.
FEES.
The Contractor agrees to pay Three Hundred Dollars ($300.00) for the
Dutcher Baseball Complex for the 2018 Season.
Payment shall be made in the form of check
payable to the City Treasurer. Payment shall be delivered or mailed to the Community Recreation
and Events, 4603 Lions Park Drive, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001. Occupation ofthe facilities by the
Contractor for any part of a year shall be deemed occupation for the entire year for the purpose of
computing user fees due under this Agreement. Payment will be due no later than October 1, 2018.
5.
SCOPE
OF WORK.
The Contractor shall provide
food
and
beverage
concessionaire services at the facility or facilities identified herein for the term identified herein.
The services to be provided are identified in the Scope of Work attached hereto as Exhibit A and
incorporated herein as if ifilly set forth.
6.
ALTERATIONS. Any remodeling or alterations of the facilities covered by this
Agreement must have the prior written approval of the City. Any remodeling or alterations which
take place without the City’s prior written approval shall, at the expense of the Contractor, be
removed and the facilities restored to their original condition if so requested by the City. At the
expiration of this Agreement, Contractor shall have the right to remove all trade fixtures incident
to the operation ofthe concession stands and placed therein by the Contractor, provided the facilities
are restored to equivalent or better condition as at the beginning of the term of this Agreement, all
without cost to the City. In so doing, any holes in the walls or floors or any other damage which
occurs incident to the removal of said trade fixtures shall be repaired to the satisfaction of the City
at the Contractor’s expense.
7.
UTILITIES. Any and all utilities including sanitation, water, sewer, and electricity
for the facilities shall be provided by the City.
Any additional utilities shall be the sole
responsibility of the Contractor.
8.
ASSIGNMENT AND SUBLETTING. The Contractor shall not assign, transfer,
mortgage, pledge, or sublet its rights under this Agreement, in whole or in part, without the prior
written consent ofthe City, provided, however, that nothing herein shall be construed to prevent the
Contractor from hiring employees to perform the actual operation of said facilities. All employees
shall be obligated to abide by the terms and conditions of this Agreement.
9.
NON-DISCRIMINATION. The Contractor hereby assures that no person shall be
excluded from participation in, be denied the benefits of, or otherwise discriminated against, in
connection with operations conducted under this Agreement on the grounds of race, color, national
origin, religion, age, pregnancy, qualiing disability, gender, or any other protected class.
