10.
DRUG ANI ALCOHOL USAGE ON CITY PROPERTY. In compliance with
the Drug Free Work Place Act ofNovember 1988, the City of Cheyenne has established an Alcohol
and Controlled Substance Policy that pertains to alcohol and drug usage by City employees. All
architects, engineers and other contractors under contract with City of Cheyenne, and their
employees and sub-contractors, are required to comply with the provisions ofthe City’s Alcohol and
Controlled Substance Policy for drug and alcohol usage on City property or other sites occupied by
the Contractor while performing the duties and responsibilities of the Agreement.
It is the
responsibility of the Contractor to be familiar with the requirements of this policy and to inform all
its employees and sub-contractors of the requirements and ensure their compliance.
If the
Contractor or its employees or sub-contractors are found in violation of this policy, the Agreement
may be terminated.
11.
COMPLIANCE WITH LAWS. The Contractor agrees that it will use the facilities
and direct its operations in accordance with all applicable local, state, and federal laws as well as
with directives of the City’s Community Recreation and Events Department, some of which may
be necessary to ensure the City’s compliance with state law, federal law, and any requirements
associated with grant funding in connection with parks facilities.
12.
SIGNS. The Contractor shall not erect, paint, or maintain any signs whatsoever
within or upon any facilities located within the parks covered by this Agreement without the prior
written permission of the City of Cheyenne Parks Manager.
13.
RIGHT OF INSPECTION AND ACCESS.
The City reserves for its officers,
employees, and authorized representatives the full and unrestricted right to enter the facilities upon
reasonable notice to the Contractor with or without the presence of the Contractor at the time of
inspection. This right also applies to access for any general maintenance requirements needs.
14.
DEFAULT, CANCELLATION, AND TERMINATION. This Agreement may
be canceled by either party for cause with thirty (30) days’ written notice to the other party. Each
and every term and condition in this Agreement shall be deemed to be a material element of the
Agreement. In the event either party should fail or refuse to perform according to the terms of this
Agreement, such party may be declared in default. In the event a party has been declared in default,
such defaulting party shall be allowed a period of fifteen (15) days within which to cure the default.
In the event the default remains uncorrected, the non-defaulting party declaring default may elect
to:
a.
Terminate the Agreement and seek damages, which damages shall not exceed
the contract amount; or
b.
Treat the Agreement as continuing and require specific performance.
15.
TAXES, LICENSES, DEBTS. The Contractor agrees to pay promptly all valid
taxes, excises, license fees, permit fees, bills, debts, and obligations incurred by it in connection with
its operation of the facilities, and not permit the same to become delinquent. The Contractor shall
not permit any lien, mortgage, judgment or execution to be filed against the facilities.
