```text
19.
WAIVERS. No waiver or default by the Contractor of any ofthe terms, covenants
or conditions hereof to be performed, kept, and observed by the Contractor shall be construed as.
or operate as, a waiver by the City of any subsequent default of any of the terms, covenants or
conditions herein contained to be performed, kept and observed by the Contractor.
20.
SURRENDER; CLEANING CHARGE.
The Contractor shall surrender the
facilities to the City at the end of each scheduled playing season in good state and condition,
reasonable wear and tear excepted. The end ofthe scheduled playing season means the last calendar
day on which an event is scheduled for that playing season. Within twenty (20) calendar days after
the end of the scheduled playing season, the Contractor shall remove all supplies, food products,
personal items, trash, and moveable equipment such as hot dog grills, coffee makers, and other
similar appliances. The Contractor shall also clean all surfaces and the floors. The failure of the
Contractor to clean the facilities in the manner and within the time limits specified herein is deemed
to be an acceptance and agreement to pay a minimum of $200.00 for cleaning charges incurred by
the City. The failure of the Contractor to remove any equipment within the twenty (20) calendar-
day period after the conclusion ofthe scheduled playing season shall result in the forfeiture of such
equipment or material without any additional notice.
Any notice provided by the City to the
Contractor to clean the facilities or to remove any equipment or material after the twenty (20) day
period following the end of the scheduled playing season shall not be deemed to be a waiver of the
City’s right to enforce the provisions contained within this numbered section of this Agreement.
21.
SPECIAL CONDITIONS.
This Agreement and all provisions hereof shall be
subject to the following special conditions.
a.
The Contractor agrees that during normally scheduled league games, and for
scheduled make-up games, the Contractor shall provide concessions during peak hours,
beginning a minimum of fifteen (15) minutes prior to the first scheduled game time and
continuing until at least forty-five (45) minutes past the start of the last scheduled games at
each facility. Game schedules will be posted via the City of Cheyenne website “Athletic
Facilities Calendars” or other similar location, but it is the duty of the Contractor to
determine the game schedules, by which their services are set.
b.
The Contractor agrees that during tournaments the Contractor shall provide
concessions during peak hours, beginning a minimum of fifteen (15) minutes prior to the
first scheduled game time and continuing until at least forty-five (45) minutes past the start
of the last scheduled games at each facility. Tournament schedules will be provided to the
Contractor by the City no later than 12:00 p.m. two (2) days prior to the start of a scheduled
tournament.
It is the duty of the Contractor to obtain a schedule of games from the
Tournament Director or such other responsible party that shall set the schedule of games for
any tournament-type event.
c.
The Contractor shall provide concessions for all hours of league operation as
specified above. The Contractor shall be required to keep themselves updated on game and
tournament schedules via the City of Cheyenne website “Athletic Facilities Calendars” or
other such source for game and tournament schedule information. Ifthe Contractor is unable
to provide concessions for any scheduled game, the Contractor shall notify the City forty-
6
